WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.707 --> 00:00:04.180
Open Twenty Cycle Check in
Dometic App Portal on your phone,

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.420
and choose English.

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.980
Enter the process you are
observing, and the station as the

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.145
subprocess.

5
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.465
Today's date is already filled in.

6
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.785
Under Standard Work CT, enter
a known cycle time in seconds

7
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.225
as your reference line.

8
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.945
If the time is unknown, enter zero.

9
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.580
Annual volume and available
production hours per week determine

10
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.145
customer takt time.

11
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.505
Enter the number of products
per cycle, usually one.

12
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.265
The calculation assumes forty-five
production weeks per year.

13
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.465
Choose the shift and check
its start and end times.

14
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.465
Enter planned stops, such as breaks,
plus the number of changeovers

15
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.145
and minutes per changeover.

16
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.065
Count each stop once.

17
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.540
These inputs provide available
running time and the basis for a

18
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.625
shift target.

19
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.620
Tap the information icon for help with a field.

20
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.905
Use a consistent cycle boundary:

21
00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.945
for example, from one press of
the machine's start button to

22
00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:57.905
the next.

23
00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.540
Tap Start in the app.

24
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.860
At each cycle boundary, tap Next cycle.

25
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.940
Timing continues immediately.

26
00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.140
On a computer, press the spacebar.

27
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.425
Measure twenty cycles and comment
on deviations, such as waiting

28
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.020
for material or an extra quality check.

29
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.140
Record the final cycle before tapping Stop.

30
00:01:17.364 --> 00:01:21.829
The results show mean cycle time,
best repeatable cycle time, B

31
00:01:21.844 --> 00:01:24.549
R C T, and disturbance rate.

32
00:01:24.564 --> 00:01:27.589
BRCT is the average of the five fastest

33
00:01:27.604 --> 00:01:28.264
cycles.

34
00:01:28.564 --> 00:01:32.344
Disturbance rate shows the
percentage gap between BRCT

35
00:01:32.404 --> 00:01:33.384
and the mean.

36
00:01:33.524 --> 00:01:37.624
Assess the suggested shift target
against real operating conditions.

37
00:01:38.307 --> 00:01:41.749
Choose PDF for a summary of
key figures, the chart and

38
00:01:41.764 --> 00:01:42.424
comments.

39
00:01:42.724 --> 00:01:46.584
Excel provides cycle data and
comments for further analysis.

40
00:01:46.724 --> 00:01:49.989
Share the file through your
phone's share menu, for example by

41
00:01:50.004 --> 00:01:51.624
email, or download it.

42
00:01:52.309 --> 00:01:54.624
Scan the QR code to open the portal.

43
00:01:54.804 --> 00:01:57.246
Measure, understand and improve.
